WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.864 --> 00:00:17.327
still can't believe nobody saw you guys sneaking out of the Cave earlier," Darb said.

2
00:00:18.108 --> 00:00:21.591
Zann and his friends were sitting at the campsite, a little apart from the adults.

3
00:00:22.331 --> 00:00:26.094
Dinner had ended an hour ago, and people were beginning to crawl into their tents for the night.

4
00:00:26.955 --> 00:00:27.616
Gliss nodded.

5
00:00:27.936 --> 00:00:29.697
"You're lucky you escaped in time.

6
00:00:30.498 --> 00:00:32.860
Why'd you pull such a risky stunt, anyway?"

7
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:34.900
Zann shot her a look.

8
00:00:35.261 --> 00:00:40.723
"I wanted to see my parents any way I could, since somebody stopped me from searching for them

9
00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:41.763
through the wormhole."

10
00:00:42.584 --> 00:00:44.905
Gliss turned away, stung by Zann's remark.

11
00:00:44.925 --> 00:00:47.246
"Zann, that was mean!"

12
00:00:47.626 --> 00:00:48.266
Perda whispered.

13
00:00:48.946 --> 00:00:49.847
Darb just frowned.

14
00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:53.608
Zann felt a twinge of guilt, though he didn't say anything.

15
00:00:54.709 --> 00:00:55.689
He knew Gliss was right.

16
00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:01.111
He, Perda, and Zing had barely made it out of range before the Sealing spell had blocked off

17
00:01:01.131 --> 00:01:02.132
that section of the Cave.

18
00:01:02.976 --> 00:01:06.237
"I didn't expect Venna to give in so quickly," Perda said.

19
00:01:06.257 --> 00:01:08.999
"I thought we'd have more time in the Cave."

20
00:01:09.759 --> 00:01:10.439
Darb shrugged.

21
00:01:10.459 --> 00:01:11.520
"What could she do?

22
00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:12.700
She got outvoted."

23
00:01:13.441 --> 00:01:16.602
Zann didn't pay much attention as the others continued to discuss the matter.

24
00:01:17.502 --> 00:01:19.823
Venna had turned over the relics she'd collected to Tok.

25
00:01:20.584 --> 00:01:24.145
He was supposed to take them deep into an unsealed section of the Cave tonight.

26
00:01:24.946 --> 00:01:26.966
Then that section would be sealed off in the morning.

27
00:01:27.707 --> 00:01:30.168
Seeing his parents' message had left Zann feeling restless.

28
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.321
Could the reference to World X, whatever that was, be a clue?

29
00:01:35.041 --> 00:01:37.102
His parents had sounded eager to find the place.

30
00:01:37.782 --> 00:01:41.903
Would they have tried to find their way there, knowing they might not make it back to Magica?

31
00:01:42.924 --> 00:01:45.784
Zann was still surprised that his parents had known Wyssa.

32
00:01:46.425 --> 00:01:47.785
Why hadn't Wyssa told him that?

33
00:01:48.485 --> 00:01:51.626
Maybe Teplo was right—maybe Zann couldn't trust anything she said.

34
00:01:51.646 --> 00:01:54.187
"It doesn't matter," he thought.

35
00:01:54.207 --> 00:01:58.168
"I can't search for my parents way out here in the middle of nowhere.

36
00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:02.886
And we'll probably head right back to Swamp Bottom once the Cave is sealed."

37
00:02:03.927 --> 00:02:05.928
He sighed with frustration and then stood up.

38
00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:08.690
"I'm tired," he told his friends.

39
00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.090
"I'm going to sleep."

40
00:02:13.112 --> 00:02:16.154
Zann woke abruptly from a confusing dream about his parents.

41
00:02:16.914 --> 00:02:20.316
All he could remember was swirling magic and a strong sense of danger.

42
00:02:21.137 --> 00:02:22.357
He sat up and looked around.

43
00:02:23.058 --> 00:02:24.559
The camp was dark and still.

44
00:02:25.279 --> 00:02:26.380
He'd been asleep for hours.

45
00:02:27.592 --> 00:02:29.974
At first Zann assumed the dream had awakened him.

46
00:02:30.714 --> 00:02:33.716
Then he heard a rustle in the scrubby trees at the edge of the camp.

47
00:02:33.736 --> 00:02:35.718
"Zing?" he whispered.

48
00:02:36.038 --> 00:02:37.619
"Leave the crawlers alone!"

49
00:02:38.439 --> 00:02:40.501
He heard a soft snore from his other side.

50
00:02:41.201 --> 00:02:45.184
Glancing that way, he saw Zing sound asleep, cuddled against Darb's side.

51
00:02:45.924 --> 00:02:49.547
The crawlers were also asleep, perched on the highest branches of the trees.

52
00:02:50.247 --> 00:02:53.409
The rustle came again, and was followed by the sound of voices.

53
00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.312
Curious, Zann got up and tiptoed toward the sound.

54
00:02:58.016 --> 00:03:02.378
Parting the tree branches, he saw Venna and Tok walking away from the campsite together.

55
00:03:03.178 --> 00:03:04.699
Their voices were low and urgent.

56
00:03:05.439 --> 00:03:07.120
Zann strained his ears to hear.

57
00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:10.382
so I've come up with a new plan," Venna was saying.

58
00:03:10.402 --> 00:03:14.363
"I know how to get those relics back to First City after all."

59
00:03:15.524 --> 00:03:17.385
Tok stopped and turned to face Venna.

60
00:03:18.105 --> 00:03:21.547
Zann crouched lower behind the trees, hoping the adults wouldn't spot him.

61
00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:22.787
"You do?"

62
00:03:23.127 --> 00:03:23.608
Tok said.

63
00:03:23.628 --> 00:03:28.803
"How? If you try to smuggle them aboard the Dragon Wagon, the furies will go crazy."

64
00:03:29.544 --> 00:03:31.025
Zann could barely believe his ears.

65
00:03:31.866 --> 00:03:33.387
Venna hadn't given in after all.

66
00:03:34.288 --> 00:03:36.370
And apparently Tok was working with her.

67
00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:39.633
"That's not my plan," Venna told Tok.

68
00:03:40.354 --> 00:03:43.456
"You'll be taking the relics into the Cave, as everyone expects.

69
00:03:44.197 --> 00:03:45.938
But you won't be leaving them there."

70
00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.681
"What?" Tok sounded confused.

71
00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:54.585
"You'll be taking those relics straight back to the capital—through the wormhole I discovered today!"

72
00:03:54.965 --> 00:03:55.986
Venna explained quickly.

73
00:03:57.046 --> 00:03:59.307
"It's deep within the western arm of the Cave.

74
00:04:00.107 --> 00:04:03.669
It must be a new one—I don't think anyone else in Magica knows about it."

75
00:04:04.469 --> 00:04:05.329
Zann was stunned.

76
00:04:05.649 --> 00:04:07.330
There was a wormhole in the Cave?

77
00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.911
"You're crazy!"

78
00:04:09.191 --> 00:04:09.851
Tok exclaimed.

79
00:04:09.871 --> 00:04:13.593
"Take some of the most powerful relics in Magica through a wormhole?

80
00:04:14.293 --> 00:04:16.914
That's much more dangerous than what I signed up for!"

81
00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:21.616
"I never expected you to lose your nerve," Venna snapped.

82
00:04:22.332 --> 00:04:25.354
"After all, this isn't your first time through a wormhole!"

83
00:04:25.374 --> 00:04:27.296
"True," Tok said.

84
00:04:27.316 --> 00:04:30.738
"But the other wormholes weren't inside the Cave of the Unknown!

85
00:04:31.519 --> 00:04:37.343
Wormholes, especially new ones, are unstable enough without adding the Cave's unpredictable energy."

86
00:04:37.363 --> 00:04:40.586
"We have to do this, Tok," said Venna.

87
00:04:40.606 --> 00:04:43.948
"The very future of Magica might depend on it!"

88
00:04:44.749 --> 00:04:45.749
She clenched her fists.

89
00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.812
"Those old fools think they're doing the right thing here.

90
00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.302
But what if another villain like Morb appears one day?

91
00:04:53.082 --> 00:04:57.465
What if a wormhole opens up right in the middle of the palace square and lets something even

92
00:04:57.485 --> 00:04:58.066
worse through?

93
00:04:58.906 --> 00:05:00.187
Magica would be helpless!"

94
00:05:01.208 --> 00:05:02.448
Tok didn't seem convinced.

95
00:05:02.469 --> 00:05:07.192
"We have plenty of magic at our disposal even without those relics.

96
00:05:08.092 --> 00:05:12.775
Boz and the others don't think it's worth the risk of having such unpredictable energy around.

97
00:05:13.856 --> 00:05:16.918
Let alone the risk of trying to take relics through a wormhole."

98
00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:18.359
He shook his head.

99
00:05:18.379 --> 00:05:19.560
"I'm sorry, Venna.

100
00:05:20.212 --> 00:05:22.614
I know you believe you're doing the right thing for Magica.

101
00:05:23.274 --> 00:05:24.575
But you'll have to do it without me.

102
00:05:24.935 --> 00:05:25.295
I'm out."

103
00:05:26.256 --> 00:05:28.017
He turned and strode back toward camp.

104
00:05:28.737 --> 00:05:31.379
Zann ducked aside just in time to avoid being seen.

105
00:05:31.399 --> 00:05:33.720
"Aargh!" Venna cried.

106
00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.942
She stormed off into the darkness in the opposite direction.

107
00:05:37.762 --> 00:05:40.424
Still in shock, Zann sat where he was for a moment.

108
00:05:41.144 --> 00:05:46.548
After seeing his parents' message—and the clue about World X—he was more eager than ever to go looking

109
00:05:46.588 --> 00:05:46.908
for them.

110
00:05:47.617 --> 00:05:50.810
And now he knew there was a wormhole somewhere in the Cave!
